        "id": 5065
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-07T17:58:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I copied GrMipLevel for this. My intent is that we would take the client data and copy it into one of these, and so in that case we\u0027d use fOptionalStorage. However, I thought there might be some internal cases where we could depend on the fPixels pointer staying alive until we snap the UploadCommand list, so that\u0027s why I left it optional.",
      "parentUuid": "95fc3dde_1f7f8684",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 27,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 27,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "d1d5158a010bedc1e13e7f9c65fd2a2de21c5438",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "eaa4c7a6_de9edcc7",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/src/UploadList.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 27,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-07T18:12:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we have the graphite image factories only take SkData, or some other ref-counting over a void*? That way we can add a ref until we\u0027re done but avoid the defensive copy?\n\nIn DrawList-\u003eDrawPass, we are able to write to GPU memory even though we aren\u0027t at the Recording snap point yet.\n\nWe don\u0027t have a more intermediate upload type between UploadList and UploadTask yet, and I\u0027m not thinking of a strong reason for one. If we had UploadList get its staging buffer and upload within the factory function, we wouldn\u0027t need this optional copy ever. But we also are spreading out the data transfer from CPU-\u003eGPU even further (maybe that\u0027s a good thing?); then the UploadTask is only responsible for creating the actual GPU texture resources that are being transferred to?",
      "parentUuid": "6c80b80b_597a8744",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 27,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 27,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "d1d5158a010bedc1e13e7f9c65fd2a2de21c5438",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2894b1be_1069a2de",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/src/UploadList.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 27,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-07T19:12:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Its not just the image factories but also the writePixels calls that will go through here (and the BackendTexture apis). For writePixels the skia API takes either an SkPixmap or SkBitmap. I like the idea of getting the stagging buffer early and immediately copying CPU data into that. I lot of the deferred uploading of CPU data in Ganesh is for DDLs/lazy proxies when we don\u0027t have access to the GPU so we may need to hold onto (possibly needing a cpu copy) for a long time. We shouldn\u0027t have that issue in graphite.",
      "parentUuid": "eaa4c7a6_de9edcc7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 27,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 27,
        "endChar": 34
      },
